  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ebola Outbreak 2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ebola Virus Disease Outbreak declared on 17 May in Eastern DR Congo and Uganda. By 19 May, about 435 suspected cases as well as 116 suspected deaths have been reported with cases speculated to be higher. It is feared that the strain of the virus, the difficult access conditions in Eastern Congo and the volatility of the context are factors which could lead to a severe large-scale outbreak.




IFRC will be launching a red level regional Emergency Appeal to support response and preparedness in neighbouring countries with a funding ask of 29M Swiss Francs.&#xa0;
We are coordinating with partners, including French RC with whom we collaborated on the Mpox response in DR Congo last year.
BRC has is also in touch with the FCDO team (TDDAP) for possible funding prospects</narrative>
  </description>
